WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.980
There are a hundred and seventy-eight laws that differentiate on the basis of sex.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:15.820
Women can't work overtime.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.420
We have to get credit cards in our husband's name.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:25.420
You think you can change the country? You should look to her generation.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:26.740
They're taking to the streets.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:30.910
Protests are important but changing the culture means nothing if the law doesn't change.

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:32.910
What did you say your name was?

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.140
Ruth Bader Ginsburg.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.300
I want to be a lawyer. I want to represent clients in pursuit of justice.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:43.000
So, they're gonna give you a corner office?

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.440
I wasn't what they were looking for.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:51.309
One said women are too emotional to be lawyers. Another told me a woman graduating top of her class must be a real ballbuster.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:53.739
I worked hard.

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:56.520
I did everything I was supposed to and I excelled.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.760
Martin Ginsburg will be signing all of our checks someday.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.380
You're a smart girl, Ruth. You married a star.

00:01:02.059 --> 00:01:07.869
If the law differentiates on the basis of sex then how will women and men ever become equal?

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:10.740
I don't read Tax Court cases.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:11.820
Read this one.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.820
The law assumes a caregiver has to be a woman.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:20.420
This is sex-based discrimination against a man.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:21.740
Poor guy.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.760
We need to take this case. This not a case, this is a declaration of war.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:30.080
He could topple the whole damn system of discrimination.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:36.510
They think gender equality is a civil right? What's at stake is the American family.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:39.280
Let's put this idea to bed once and for all.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:43.040
You will lose and when you do you will set the women's movement back ten years.

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:45.140
You don't get to tell me when to quit.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:47.620
I know this case disrupted our lives.

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.700
Who's it for? If not for me?

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:00.880
You've been ready for this your whole life.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.380
So, go in there and let the judges see the Ruth Ginsburg I know.

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:07.740
We're not asking you to change the country.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:09.930
That's already happened without any court's permission.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:20.022
The word woman does not appear even once in the US Constitution.

00:02:20.022 --> 00:02:21.910
Nor does the word freedom.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:25.420
Your honor.

